{"nodes": [{"id": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___option_c_explained_6fcd99e1", "label": "Self-roster Fairness - Option C Explained", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "graphify-out/converted/Self-roster Fairness - Option C Explained_6fcd99e1.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___option_c_explained_6fcd99e1_option_c", "label": "Option C - Preference Week + Fair Draw", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "graphify-out/converted/Self-roster Fairness - Option C Explained_6fcd99e1.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Designed to remove both the race and the feeling of one: a sealed 7-day preference window where timing is irrelevant; uncontested picks are simply granted, contested slots go first to priority points then to an audited seeded draw; draw losers gain a carry-over point so the system self-corrects (it owes you next time, automatically and visibly). Every allocation carries a one-line receipt. Trade-offs: results arrive at the deadline rather than instantly; contested losers visibly miss the day they wanted (but gain priority); a small new habit to learn; modest setup needed. Recommended by the Director Brief as the best fit for the group."}, {"id": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___option_c_explained_6fcd99e1_priority_points_carry_over", "label": "Priority Points Carry-over", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "graphify-out/converted/Self-roster Fairness - Option C Explained_6fcd99e1.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Designed as the system's memory so luck evens out: lose a draw and you gain +1 point usable from the very next contested draw; points never expire and carry across cycles; they reset only when they have done their job (winning a contested slot); uncontested slots never touch them. By construction whoever has the worst luck this cycle is first in line next time - equity without negotiation."}, {"id": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___option_c_explained_6fcd99e1_ua_budget", "label": "UA Cannot-Work Budget", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "graphify-out/converted/Self-roster Fairness - Option C Explained_6fcd99e1.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "UA days are capped (about one per three shifts owed, rounded up, minimum 6, auto-adjusted for leave) precisely so an accepted UA can be guaranteed never overridden by draw or auto-fill. A zone-aware coverage floor stops a day accepting UA once the eligible pool would drop to minimum staffing plus a margin; oversubscribed UA is decided by draw and carry-over at window close, never by who marked first. Unlimited free prefer-not marks exist so UA is saved for genuine cannots, and leave is kept separate so it never consumes the budget."}, {"id": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___option_c_explained_6fcd99e1_draw_receipts", "label": "Audited Draw Receipts", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "graphify-out/converted/Self-roster Fairness - Option C Explained_6fcd99e1.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every placement carries its reason - uncontested grants, priority wins, seeded re-checkable draws, auto-fills, rare prefer-not use, zone steering - in an append-only log visible to all, so nobody has to trust the process: anyone can look, and the answer to why didn't I get the 15th is the same record a month later."}, {"id": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___option_c_explained_6fcd99e1_zone_profiles", "label": "Zone Profiles and Constrained-First Placement", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "graphify-out/converted/Self-roster Fairness - Option C Explained_6fcd99e1.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The ballot deliberately stays about days - nobody marks zones. Admin-set profiles (eligible zones, percentage targets) drive zone-by-zone capacity underneath; most-constrained staff are placed first, dissolving most clashes without a draw; percentage targets balance across the cycle rather than day by day; auto-fill respects eligibility and flags impossible cover to the admin; a scarce-skill guardrail warns before the last cover for a zone goes unavailable, and draw records show zone scope so nobody wonders why a colleague was not in the draw."}, {"id": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___option_c_explained_6fcd99e1_fixed_flexible_layering", "label": "Fixed-First Roster Layering", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "graphify-out/converted/Self-roster Fairness - Option C Explained_6fcd99e1.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fixed patterns are stamped first so nothing changes for fixed-pattern colleagues - their trade-off (certainty instead of choice) was settled when the pattern was agreed. Flexible staff contest only the remaining capacity, fully-filled days show as full so nobody wastes a mark or enters a draw for a slot that does not exist, and priority points are deliberately a flexible-staff-only ledger while the equity view still counts everyone's tough shifts. A fixed colleague's leave returns slots to the pool; hybrids go through preference week for their flexible remainder. Every option A-E keeps this layering."}], "edges": [{"source": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___option_c_explained_6fcd99e1", "target": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___option_c_explained_6fcd99e1_option_c", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "graphify-out/converted/Self-roster Fairness - Option C Explained_6fcd99e1.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___option_c_explained_6fcd99e1", "target": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___option_c_explained_6fcd99e1_priority_points_carry_over", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "graphify-out/converted/Self-roster Fairness - Option C Explained_6fcd99e1.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___option_c_explained_6fcd99e1", "target": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___option_c_explained_6fcd99e1_ua_budget", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "graphify-out/converted/Self-roster Fairness - Option C Explained_6fcd99e1.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___option_c_explained_6fcd99e1", "target": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___option_c_explained_6fcd99e1_draw_receipts", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "graphify-out/converted/Self-roster Fairness - Option C Explained_6fcd99e1.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___option_c_explained_6fcd99e1", "target": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___option_c_explained_6fcd99e1_zone_profiles", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "graphify-out/converted/Self-roster Fairness - Option C Explained_6fcd99e1.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___option_c_explained_6fcd99e1", "target": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___option_c_explained_6fcd99e1_fixed_flexible_layering", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "graphify-out/converted/Self-roster Fairness - Option C Explained_6fcd99e1.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___option_c_explained_6fcd99e1_priority_points_carry_over", "target": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___option_c_explained_6fcd99e1_option_c", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "graphify-out/converted/Self-roster Fairness - Option C Explained_6fcd99e1.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___option_c_explained_6fcd99e1_ua_budget", "target": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___option_c_explained_6fcd99e1_option_c", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "graphify-out/converted/Self-roster Fairness - Option C Explained_6fcd99e1.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___option_c_explained_6fcd99e1_draw_receipts", "target": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___option_c_explained_6fcd99e1_option_c", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "graphify-out/converted/Self-roster Fairness - Option C Explained_6fcd99e1.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___option_c_explained_6fcd99e1_zone_profiles", "target": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___option_c_explained_6fcd99e1_option_c", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "graphify-out/converted/Self-roster Fairness - Option C Explained_6fcd99e1.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___option_c_explained_6fcd99e1_fixed_flexible_layering", "target": "graphify_o